ENTRY            D1095   20260628   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D1095001   20260628   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                  9         33
TITLE      Direct measurement of the 7Li(p,alpha)4He reaction at
            astrophysical energies using the ELISSA array
AUTHOR     (H.Pai, G.L.Guardo, Sk M.Ali, I.Kuncser, A.Lupoae,
            T.Petruse, C.Matei, Y.Xu, S.Aogaki, D.L.Balabanski,
            S.R.Ban, M.Brezeanu, A.Cassisa, M.La Cognata,
            A.Cvetinovic, A.Dhal, P.Figuera, A.Kusoglu, L.Lamia,
            D.Lattuada, V.Lelasseux, O.E.Lopez-Lopez, C.A.Marin,
            C.V.Nedelcu, A.Pappalardo, I.P.Parlea, R.G.Pizzone,
            G.M.Restifo, R.Roy, P.-A.Soederstroem, S.Niculae,
            N.T.Szegedi, V.A.Toma, A.Tumino, G.Turturica, T.Tozar,
            N.Vukman)
INSTITUTE  (3RUMBUC,2ITYLNS,1USATAM,3RUMBUU,3CZRUJF,3SLNIJS,
            2TUKSTU,2ITYCAT,2ITYSIC,2ITYENN,3MEXUMX,3INDIIR,
            3CRORBZ)
           (3RUMRUM) University Politehnica of Bucharest
           (3CROCRO) University of Split, Split
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,045804,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/hlq9-7fyd
FACILITY   (CYCTM,3RUMBUC) 3 MV Tandetron Accelerator
SAMPLE     A self-supported polyethylene (CH2) target with a
            thickness of about 70 ug/cm2, placed at 90 degree to
            the 7Li beam with an average beam intensity ~2-4 pnA.
DETECTOR   (SISD) ELISSA array having 12 X3 position-sensitive
            strip detectors were placed at a distance of ~6 cm
            from the target cente.
            The angular resolution for the present X3 detectors
            is ~0.3-0.5 degree.
           (SI) A silicon monitor detector (active area: 25 mm2)
            was placed at a scattering angle of 27.6 degree and
            a distance of 150 mm from the target.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by H.Pai (2026-07-03)
HISTORY    (20260528R) VT. Data received from H.Pai (2026-05-28)
           (20260628C) VT
ENDBIB              33
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           36
SUBENT        D1095002   20260628   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                  3          6
REACTION   ((1-H-1(3-LI-7,A)2-HE-4,,DA)=
           (3-LI-7(P,A)2-HE-4,,DA))
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Uncertainties arise from statistical
            uncertainty and the solid angle uncertainties of the
            monitor and X3 detectors.
STATUS     (TABLE,,H.Pai+,J,PR/C,113,045804,2026) Fig.2
ENDBIB               6
